	(text "AI GENERATED: \nFor a network consisting of 150 CAN FD transceivers, the aggregate bus loading must be considered to ensure that the transceivers can maintain adequate differential output voltage. \nUsing the TI TCAN1476-Q1 as an example, which has a minimum differential input resistance of 40 kΩ, the equivalent resistance of 150 transceivers connected in parallel is \\(R_{\\text{nodes}}=40\\,000/150=266.7\\ \\Omega\\). \nWith two 120 Ω termination resistors connected at either end of the bus, the equivalent termination resistance is \\(R_{\\text{termination}}=120\\parallel120=60\\ \\Omega\\). \nTherefore, the total equivalent bus resistance is \\(R_{\\text{bus}}=60\\parallel266.7=\\boxed{49.0\\ \\Omega}\\). \nSince the TCAN1476-Q1 specifies operation with a minimum differential load resistance of 45 Ω, the calculated 49.0 Ω load is theoretically within its specified operating conditions. \nAdditionally, with a maximum input capacitance of 20 pF per bus pin, 150 transceivers contribute up to \\(150\\times20=3\\text{ nF}\\) of input capacitance per bus conductor. \nAlthough the resistive loading is acceptable, the cumulative capacitance and physical bus layout should also be evaluated to ensure reliable communication across all 150 devices.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.212 -10.922 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d06bd463-59bb-480b-b2bf-a30e417bce23")
	)
